    Bug 2046866 - Port bug 2040339: Fix tabs.getCurrent() throwing "Not implemented". r=john.bieling,robwu

    The upstream bug introduced a new abstract
    TabTrackerBase.getTabForBrowser(browser) method in ext-tabs-base.js.
    Thunderbird's TabTracker did not override it, causing
    browser.tabs.getCurrent() to throw "Not implemented".

    The fix adds the missing override, delegating to
    tabmail.getTabForBrowser(browser), and falls back to returning the
    window for standalone/secondary windows.

    Following the upstream cleanup, the _browsers cache and
    getBrowserTabId method are removed.  Callers now use
    getTabForBrowser + getId directly.

    A test is included to verify getCurrent() returns the correct tab
    when called from an extension page loaded in a content tab.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306204

